hi there steve here again to talk about  language learning  and today i'm going to talk about  sort of  the strategy  what is the strategy  that you need to have to learn another  language  this is something that i've gradually  gotten used to  um when i was 20 when i um had just  finished learning french and was about  to learn chinese  you know i never thought that at the age  of 72  i would be trying to learn arabic and  farsi and that these would be my  whatever it is 16 17 18 languages i  never would have thought that was  possible  i have gotten used to the idea  that i can learn any language i want  what's more i've come to realize that  i learn by not learning or by not  studying in other words the process is  one of getting used to another language  developing habits in another language in  the previous video i spoke about  you know the subjunctive and that it's  not a matter of understanding the theory  of when we use the subjunctive although  that is certainly part of what we do but  we can't remember those  explanations those rules we can't  remember the different endings  but with enough exposure to the language  we start to get used to these patterns  of the other language  so i noticed myself for example when i  see the meaning of a word so i'm  learning on link and i look up a word  and there's a dictionary definition  there  which may or may not be suitable to my  context because very often the  dictionary definition doesn't work or  maybe the word was misspelled or any  number of things could  you know give me an answer  a meaning for that word that doesn't  suit  it never bothers me  because i know from experience  that until i see that word in many  different situations  until i get used to that word i really  won't know how to use it and i i really  won't know its meaning or the scope of  its meaning and which words it's used  together with  so it's not a matter of learning stuff  studying stuff it in isolation it's it's  a matter of giving yourself enough  opportunity so that the brain can start  to get used to  a different approach so  right now with my farsi i'm listening to  it i'm getting a better sense of the  sounds i think i can clearly tell when  one word ends and the next word begins  i've got a few words  the system tells me i know 50 words or  something  uh very early in the game but i just  know that with enough time with enough  reading and listening i will get used to  farsi just as i got used to greek and  ukrainian and now in my arabic for  example  um we have this wonderful version of who  is she that was created for me by  someone that i found on upwork  and i i listened to it i understand it  and it's it's music to my ears it's so  pleasantly uh narrated  and i know that even if i keep  forgetting words that this is just part  of this process of getting used to  another language developing new habits  and we develop these new habits  you know  subconsciously in a way and and i am  very confident now  that  with enough exposure with enough reading  and listening i will get used to  another language i can get used to any  language turkish finnish mongolian  swahili it doesn't matter  now  again you know some people maybe think  older people can't learn languages  when i was 20 i didn't have that  attitude i didn't have the attitude that  i can simply  learn any language as long as i give my  brain the opportunity  by enough exposure  you know give my brain the opportunity  to get used to a new language to develop  new neural connections to deal with a  new language as long as i do that and as  long as i want to get this language in  me i can do it any language and this is  the way i feel now it's certainly not  how i felt when i was in my teens when  it seemed like  learning a new language was very  difficult i was confronted with you know  conjunction at least conjugation tables  declension tables rules and it just  seemed like a real struggle whereas i  now realize that it's a very gradual  process  of getting used to something so the  strategy in language learning should be  to ignore tests  to not worry about what you forget not  worry about what you understand you know  understand or don't understand and just  focus on letting yourself get used to  the new language so that's the strategy  i hope this makes sense bye for now  [Music]  you
 

